                    <line x1="220" y1="424" x2="660" y2="424" stroke="#A8442B" stroke-width="3"/>
                    {# Ground line — long olive #}
                    <line x1="0" y1="450" x2="720" y2="450" stroke="#6E6E3C" stroke-width="2"/>
                    {# Plate corner mark — small architectural notation #}
                    <g fill="#6E6E3C" font-family="Khand, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="2">
                        <text x="20" y="510">FIG. 01 — BUTTERFLY ROOF · BATANGAS BUNGALOW · 2pt OLIVE</text>
                    </g>
                </svg>
            </div>

            {# Cols 8–12: folio label + Recoleta italic H1 + deck #}
            <div class="hero__text">
                <p class="folio">Folio 01 / 2026 <span class="square-mark"></span> Section I</p>
                <h1 class="hero__h1">Bahay,<br>anyo,<br><em>hangin.</em></h1>
                <p class="hero__deck hero__deck--ink">Anyo at Disenyo is a Batangas architectural practice designing homes and small buildings shaped by Philippine light, climate, and the way a family actually lives in a room.</p>
                <p>
                    <a class="btn" href="/inquiry">Make an inquiry</a>
                    &nbsp; &nbsp;
                    <a class="btn--ghost" href="/work">See the folio</a>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        {# Terracotta 4pt rule — fingerprint #2 #}
        <hr class="rule-4">
    </div>
</section>

{# ── SECTION I — WHAT WE DO ─────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section class="section section--lg">
    <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Section I <span class="square-mark"></span> Anyo at Disenyo</p>
        <h2 style="max-width: 16ch;">What we do, and how we do it.</h2>
        <div class="what-we-do">
            <div class="what-we-do__lhs">
                <span>Hangin.</span>
                <span class="tagalog">Liwanag.</span>
                <span>Lilim.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="what-we-do__rhs">
                <p>We are a small, owner-led architectural office working from Batangas City. Our work is residential and small-commercial — single-family houses, a rebuild for a sari-sari shop on the corner, a clinic for a doctor returning from Manila — built for the Philippine climate first and the brief second.</p>
                <p>Every project begins on the site. We read where the morning sun lands, where the afternoon rain comes in, where the family already sits when nothing is asked of them. The plan grows from those observations. The drawings are calm. The materials are local. We work on a small number of projects each year, in person, with the people who will live in the house.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <hr class="rule-1">
    </div>
</section>

{# ── SECTION II — SELECTED WORK (3 plates) — fingerprint #5 ─────── #}
<section class="section section--lg" style="background: var(--coconut);">
    <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Section II <span class="square-mark"></span> Folio</p>
